    {"claim": "Incumbents already hold the first-party data troves, so siloing mandates don't shrink their surveillance footprint — they shrink everyone else's training substrate.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "If Congress wants threshold-triggered scrutiny, the precondition is anti-capture institutional design — rotating membership, sunset clauses, and structural separation of halt from licensing — not a footnote.", "targets": []}
  ],
  "key_assumptions": [
