    {"assumption": "Anti-capture institutional design — rotation, sunsets, separation of powers — is implementable in statute and survives lobbying pressure.", "if_wrong": "If those safeguards become nominal in practice, any threshold-triggered audit regime becomes an incumbent shield, and the defensible path collapses to disclosure-only scaffolding enforced through private rights of action rather than agency gatekeeping."}
