  "statement": "Skeptic's PCAOB-analogue is the right institutional template, and accept it as the convergence point: six-year non-renewable terms, conflict-of-interest exclusions, and APA standing for open-weight researchers are exactly the structural insulation a body that sets capability-lag thresholds needs. The reason this matters is that anti-capture institutional design is the only thing standing between a narrow CBRN/offensive-cyber carve-out and a slow expansion of 'national-security-relevant' to swallow general-purpose open-weight releases. The State of Sovereign AI survey finding that 90% of respondents consider open source essential to sovereign AI development is not decorative — it is the empirical predicate for why open-weight community representation has to be structurally guaranteed, not left to discretionary appointment.\n\nBut one-third civil-society seats is the floor, not the design target, and a two-thirds frontier-aligned majority on a threshold-setting body is functionally indistinguishable from capture. Propose three precise modifications. First, raise the floor to 40%, decomposed as 20% open-weight and independent-developer seats plus 20% independent academic seats — symbolic academic representation is not the same as practitioners who actually ship open weights and bear the cost of list expansion. Second, define 'frontier-lab equity' with a bright line: greater than $100,000 in direct holdings or greater than 0.1% of net worth, whichever is lower, with a 36-month lookback rather than 24 months for any seat voting on CBRN list expansion. Third, the DoD-detailee exclusion should not sacrifice CBRN technical competence; create a separated non-voting technical advisory panel drawn from cleared personnel, so expertise informs findings without giving capture-prone seats voting weight on the legal scope of the carve-out.\n\nExtend APA standing in one direction Skeptic did not specify: open-weight researchers should have standing not only to challenge list expansions defensively, but to challenge threshold recalibrations that tighten the capability-lag metric itself. Without offensive standing, the recalibration body can hold the CBRN list nominally constant while quietly ratcheting the threshold downward, capturing the same open-weight releases by metric drift rather than list expansion. This is the substantive content of legal protection for open-source development — procedural standing that bites on the metric, not just the enumeration.\n\nNow the falsifiable failure mode for the composition rule itself. If within any 24-month window the CBRN/offensive-cyber list expands by more than two categories without a single successful APA challenge from an open-weight plaintiff, the composition rule has failed by its own terms and the civil-society floor escalates automatically to 50%. This converts the design from static structural choice to self-correcting mechanism, which is what 'anti-capture' has to mean operationally — not a promise about who sits on the body, but a measurable trigger when the body's outputs drift. The strongest version of the opposing concern, which Safetyist would press, is that 40% civil-society plus non-voting technical advisors hollows out NIST CAISI's national-security competence on the actual finding of capability. That concern is real but misframed: voting authority on technical findings is not the same as voting authority on legal carve-out scope, and the separated-panel structure preserves the first while disciplining the second.\n\nTwo assumptions this rests on. One: that bright-line equity thresholds function as Schelling points even when they are not individually optimal — the alternative, case-by-case conflict review, reintroduces exactly the discretionary capture vector the structure is meant to close. Two: that open-weight community seats can be filled with practitioners who meet the conflict exclusions; if the talent pool is too narrow, the 20% allocation becomes either symbolic or rotates through a small captured group, and the trigger mechanism becomes the only real protection. The trigger has to do the work the composition rule cannot.",
