er-tier overreach dressed as jurisdictional closure — Accelerationist is right that domestic deployment is the hook, and the cost on small and foreign open-weight researchers is real. I preserve only the narrow CBRN/offensive-cyber gate, and I relocate the entire remaining disagreement to one question the other two parties must now answer: who sits on the recalibration body, under what tenure rules, and with what standing rights for outside challengers? That is the last real joint in this structure. Everything else has converged.",
